## 2. Functional Conception & Module Boundaries

The system is organized into eight interconnected operational pillars acting as isolated bounded contexts. Modules do not share database schemas directly but communicate via synchronous internal API ports for read queries and an asynchronous Event Bus (Apache Kafka) for state mutations.

```mermaid
graph TD
    UI[React JS / Mapbox UI] --> API[Spring Boot API Gateway & Security]
    
    subgraph Relational & Transactional Domain
        IAM[Identity & Security]
        PROC[Procurement & Acquisition]
        PLAN[Topography & Planning]
        CMDB[CMDB & Inventory]
        TOPO[Topology & QoS]
        ITSM[Maintenance & ITSM]
    end
    
    subgraph High-Frequency & Analytical Domain
        TELE[Telemetry & Monitoring]
        AI[AI Analytics & Digital Twin]
    end

    API --> IAM
    API --> PROC
    API --> PLAN
    API --> CMDB
    API --> TOPO
    API --> ITSM
    API --> TELE
    API --> AI
    
    %% Event Bus Integrations
    TELE -.->|Kafka Events| TOPO
    TELE -.->|Kafka Events| ITSM
    PLAN -.->|Kafka Events| PROC
    PROC -.->|Kafka Events| CMDB
    
    %% Databases
    db1[(PostgreSQL Relational)]
    db2[(TimescaleDB Time-Series)]
    
    IAM --> db1
    PROC --> db1
