    CMDB --> db1
    TOPO --> db1
    ITSM --> db1
    
    TELE --> db2
    AI --> db1
    AI --> db2

```

### 2.1 Identity & Security Module (IAM/MLS)

* **Boundary:** Solely responsible for authentication, authorization, Multi-Level Security (MLS) clearances, cryptographic key management, and ABAC policy evaluations.

### 2.2 Topography & Deployment Planning Module

* **Boundary:** Controls GIS coordinates, Line-of-Sight (LoS) RF link budgets, civil infrastructure specs (towers, power), and site rollout project management. Enforces rules ensuring every new `EDGE_SITE` connects back to a `REGIONAL_DISTRIBUTION` or `BACKBONE_CORE` node.

### 2.3 End-to-End Procurement Module

* **Boundary:** Manages the statutory financial lifecycle: Purchase Requisitions, Budget Commitments, Tender Bidding, Contracts, Purchase Orders (POs), Goods Receipts (GRNs), and Invoices.

### 2.4 CMDB & Warehouse Inventory Module

* **Boundary:** The physical hardware ledger. Tracks `Asset` lifecycles, MAC addresses, modular chassis relationships, configuration baselines, and stock movements.

### 2.5 Topology & QoS Module

* **Boundary:** The logical networking plane. Maps active IP configurations, `RedundancyGroup` failover paths, layer-1/layer-2 transmission links, and partitions physical link capacity into hard Quality of Service (QoS) queues (`VOICE`, `VISIOPHONE`, `DATA`).

### 2.6 Telemetry & Real-Time Monitoring Module

* **Boundary:** High-frequency ingestor utilizing Spring Virtual Threads for ICMP/SNMP polling. Executes thousands of concurrent health checks and evaluates thresholds without locking the relational hub.

### 2.7 ITSM & Maintenance Module

* **Boundary:** Manages human field operations: Trouble Tickets, Field Work Orders, Preventive Maintenance schedules, and RMA returns to vendors.

### 2.8 AI Analytics & Simulation Engine (Digital Twin)

* **Boundary:** Isolated Python-based microservice. Ingests historical data to train predictive maintenance models, generate vendor reliability scores, and execute memory-heavy graph computations for synthetic fault simulations (e.g., simulating a blackout in a specific wilaya).

