## 4. Core Integration & Process Flows

Data fluidity across the Hexagonal architecture is managed via synchronous internal API ports for reads and the Kafka Event Bus for state mutations.

### 4.1 Validated Deployment to Hardware Ingestion (Procurement Flow)

From the moment architects plan a site to the moment hardware enters the warehouse.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Plan as Topography & Planning
    participant CMDB as CMDB & Inventory
    participant Kafka as Event Bus (Kafka)
    participant Proc as Procurement
    participant Whse as Warehouse Operations

    Plan->>CMDB: Sync Query: Check AssetAvailabilityPort
    CMDB-->>Plan: Return Shortfall (Missing hardware)
    Plan->>Kafka: Publish SiteBOMValidatedEvent
    Kafka-->>Proc: Consume Event
    Proc->>Proc: Generate Purchase Requisition & Tender
    Note over Proc: Tender Awarded & PO Issued
    Proc->>Whse: Await physical delivery
    Whse->>Proc: Submit GoodsReceiptNote & QA Inspection
    Proc->>Kafka: Publish GoodsReceiptInspectedEvent
    Kafka-->>CMDB: Consume Event
    CMDB->>CMDB: Provision new Asset entities (Status: IN_STOCK)

```

### 4.2 Autonomous Telemetry to Failover & ITSM

A critical, low-latency automated flow requiring microsecond interactions to protect `VOICE` and `VISIOPHONE` QoS queues.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Telemetry as Telemetry & Monitoring
    participant TSDB as TimescaleDB
    participant Topo as Topology & QoS
    participant Kafka as Event Bus (Kafka)
    participant ITSM as Maintenance Module

    Telemetry->>TSDB: Ingest NodeMetrics (High Frequency)
    Telemetry->>Telemetry: Evaluate Threshold (e.g., Loss of Signal)
    Telemetry->>Topo: Sync Query: RedundancyPathLookupPort(LinkID)
    Topo-->>Telemetry: Return Secondary Backup Link Details
    Telemetry->>Telemetry: Execute Automated Reroute Script
    Telemetry->>Kafka: Publish LinkFailoverExecutedEvent
    
    par Update Topology State
        Kafka-->>Topo: Consume Event
        Topo->>Topo: Update RedundancyGroup (is_failover_active = true)
    and Dispatch Maintenance
        Kafka-->>ITSM: Consume Event
        ITSM->>ITSM: Generate Critical TroubleTicket
        ITSM->>ITSM: Dispatch FieldWorkOrder to NOC
    end

```

### 4.3 AI Analytics & Crisis Simulation (Digital Twin)

The proactive process allowing leadership to test survivability before real-world events occur.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Cmd as Command Unit
    participant AI as AI & Simulation Engine
    participant DBs as Relational & TSDB Hubs
    participant Kafka as Event Bus (Kafka)
    participant Plan as Topography & Planning

    Cmd->>AI: Initiate SimulationScenario (e.g., Regional Blackout)
    AI->>DBs: Pull live Topology Graph & Historical Metrics
    DBs-->>AI: Return Digital Twin baseline
    AI->>AI: Inject Synthetic Faults (Sever virtual links)
    AI->>AI: Compute Cascading Impacts & QoS bottlenecks
    AI->>Kafka: Publish SimulationResultGeneratedEvent
    Kafka-->>Plan: Consume Event
    Plan->>Plan: Flag vulnerable sites for physical redundancy upgrades

```

