## 5. Technology Stack & Infrastructure Rules

| Domain | Core Technology | Architectural Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Client Presentation** | React JS (TypeScript) | Delivers a Single Page Application (SPA) utilizing Mapbox for GIS planning and WebSockets for pushing millisecond-latency telemetry alerts to operators. |
| **API & Business Logic** | Spring Boot (Java) | Serves as the central engine enforcing unit-based security (`Planning`, `Procurement`, `Maintenance`), executing complex topology rules, and managing PO transitions via Spring State Machine. |
| **Telemetry Worker** | Spring WebFlux / Virtual Threads | Executes thousands of non-blocking, concurrent network polling requests directly from within the Spring ecosystem. |
| **AI & Sim Runtime** | Python (FastAPI, PyTorch) | Microservice dedicated strictly to graph computations, statistical reliability scoring, and predictive forecasting. |
| **Relational Hub** | PostgreSQL (Spring Data JPA) | Enforces strict referential integrity for complex hardware inventories, geographical coordinates, vendor contracts, and physical interface connections. |
| **Monitoring Hub** | TimescaleDB | A time-series database optimized for high-volume, append-only writes. Ingests timestamped node metrics without locking PostgreSQL. |
| **Event Broker** | Apache Kafka | Functions as the central nervous system, consuming module events and instantly broadcasting failover commands, PO generation, and simulation updates. |
